OLAP (Online Analytical Processing)

What is OLAP?

OLAP is a technology and approach used to analyze data quickly across multiple dimensions.
It supports complex analytical queries, not inserts/updates.

Why OLAP?

Fast aggregation (SUM, COUNT, AVG)
Slice, Dice, Drill-down, Roll-up
Business-friendly analysis

When is OLAP used?

Reporting
Dashboards
Ad-hoc analysis
Trend comparison

Where is OLAP used?

On top of a Data Warehouse
BI tools
OLAP cubes (SSAS, Snowflake, BigQuery)

How OLAP works?

Data is organized in facts and dimensions, enabling:
Drill down (Year → Month → Day)
Slice (only Cardiology patients)
  Dice (Cardiology + 2024 + Oregon)

Healthcare Scenario

We used OLAP to analyze patient visits by year, month, department, and provider.
Executives could drill down from hospital-level metrics to individual physicians to identify performance and quality gaps.
