Facts

What is a Fact?

A fact represents a measurable business event. after measuring we can take the decision based on that report. 
It answers How many? How much?

Why Facts?

Store metrics used for analysis
Central point for reporting

When used?

Whenever business wants numeric analysis.

Where stored?
In fact tables.

How are they designed?

Contains foreign keys to dimensions
Contains measures
Usually very large tables

Example Fact Table (Healthcare)

Fact_Patient_Visit

Column	Description
Patient_SK	FK
Provider_SK	FK
Date_SK	FK
Visit_Count	1
Visit_Cost	1200

Healthcare Scenario

I worked on Fact_Claims and Fact_Encounters, capturing visit counts, charges, reimbursements, and length of stay, which were later used to calculate KPIs like cost per patient and readmission rates.
