Surrogate Key

What is a Surrogate Key?

A surrogate key is a system-generated key (usually integer) used in the Data Warehouse instead of business keys.

Why Surrogate Keys?

Source system keys change
Faster joins
Supports history (SCD Type 2)
Decouples DW from source systems

When used?

Always in dimension tables.

Where used?

As primary key in dimension tables and foreign key in fact tables.

How created?

Auto-increment
Sequence
Identity column

Example

Patient Dimension

Patient_SK	Patient_ID (Business Key)	Name
101	 	MRN123				John
102		MRN123				John (new address)

Healthcare Scenario

I implemented surrogate keys for Patient and Provider dimensions to track historical changes without losing old records, especially important for regulatory and audit reporting.
