Business Key

What is a Business Key?

A business key is a unique identifier coming from the source system.

Why Business Keys?

Identify records in source systems
Used for data integration
Required during ETL to find matches

When used?

During ETL
For deduplication
Source-to-target mapping

Where used?

Stored in dimension tables
Not recommended as fact table FK

Example Business Keys (Healthcare)
Entity	Business Key
Patient	MRN
Provider	NPI
Claim	Claim Number

Healthcare Scenario

During ETL, I used MRN and NPI as business keys to identify patients and providers from multiple source systems, then generated surrogate keys to maintain consistency inside the warehouse.

One-Line Memory Trick (Very Important)

Business keys identify records in the real world; surrogate keys identify records inside the Data Warehouse.

Facts measure events, dimensions describe them, OLAP analyzes them, and the Data Warehouse stores them all historically.
