Q What is archive dimension?

An Archive Dimension is used in a Data Warehouse to store old or inactive dimension records that are no longer required for day-to-day analysis but must be kept for historical, audit, or compliance purposes. This helps reduce the size of active dimension tables and improves query performance.

Healthcare Example

In a healthcare data warehouse, consider a Provider Dimension that stores doctor details. Providers who retired or left the organization 10+ years ago are rarely needed for regular reporting. Instead of keeping them in the active Provider dimension, these records are moved to an Archive Dimension.

We just transfer the data from the online mode to offline mode (in DVDs, Floppy disk, CD, Hard disk)
